filenumber 632883
! *** DO NOT RUN -- DOMAIN TOO SMALL, job cancelled ***
! At 17.2 d the pressure front reaches 5.17 km against a half-domain of
! 6.01 km (86%), so the Dirichlet boundaries begin draining it. Kept only
! for reference. Use res632880/res632881 (5.00 d, 2.79 km = 46%) instead,
! or rebuild on a >=691x691 grid before running to 17 d or beyond.
! FULL-INJECTION reference run -- Wang & Dunham's parameters, dc 1e-4.
! Identical to res632881.in except tmax: 17.20 d instead of 5.00 d.
!
! 17.20 d is the end of injection (the rate record goes to zero at 17.15 d),
! not the end of the 31.39 d file. Two reasons to stop there:
!   - everything after is shut-in, and HBI has no wellbore bleed-off, so it
!     cannot follow a shut-in at all (simulated wellhead stays near its
!     flowing value while the measurement drops ~20 MPa).
!   - the domain is 601 x 0.020 km = +/-6.01 km, and with Taiyi's far-field
!     D = 4.49 m2/s the diffusion length is 5.17 km at 17.2 d but 6.90 km at
!     30.66 d. The Dirichlet boundaries (pbcl/r/t/b 0) would drain the
!     pressure past ~25 d. Taiyi's own domain is +/-10 km.
! Even at 17.2 d the front is at 86% of the half-domain, so the far field is
! becoming boundary-influenced -- worth stating alongside any result.
problem 3dp
imax 601
jmax 601
ds 0.020
interval 30
nstep 400000
tmax 0.04712329
dtmax 43200
dtout 0.0002
parameterfromfile T
parameter_file "perm_taiyi_601_ds20.txt"
parameter_file_ncol 1
backslip T
vpl 0d0
a 0.015
b 0.012
dc 1e-4
f0 0.6
muinit 0.5359
sigmainit 27.99
velinit 1d-12
limitsigma T
minsig 1
velmin 1d-20
pressurediffusion T
permev F
kp 4e-13
phi 0.01
beta 1e-8
eta 0.89e-3
kL 1e-3
kT 1e15
pfinit 0d0
bcl Dirichlet
bcr Dirichlet
bct Dirichlet
bcb Dirichlet
pbcl 0d0
pbcr 0d0
pbct 0d0
pbcb 0d0
injectionfromfile T
injection_file "june_clean.txt"
rigid 24
Sw_fwid 7.4e-9
rw 8.9e-2
